	filename: "stuck_in_the_burb"
	title: "Stuck in the BURB"
	subtitle: ["MOD : Minestuck"]
	default_quest_shape: ""
	default_hide_dependency_lines: false
	quests: [
		{
			title: "Remnants of a Lost Game"
			x: -4.75d
			y: -2.5d
			shape: "square"
			subtitle: "MOD : Minestuck"
			description: [
				"&7You have found something... quite interesting."
				""
				"&7Right now, the bosses are helping you break out of the system, while myself and the other Researchers are helping you survive until then."
				""
				"&7But what you just found? Might be just the thing that will help ALL of us. Especially you."
			]
			dependencies: ["14E05D152CF5C051"]
			id: "2019F6F56C5A7D4B"
			tasks: [{
				id: "387B7D9AC801F060"
				type: "item"
				item: "minestuck:raw_cruxite"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Lost in the System"
			x: -3.5d
			y: -2.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7Okay, Bandit, the thing you found is called Cruxite. It's... hm, where should I begin."
				""
				"&7Well, long before the FOP and their Game Server, with it's Advent of Ascension core game, there used to be another game. Nobody knows who made it, but it was as expansive as the FOP Game Server. The game was known as SBurb. "
				""
				"&7Four or so years after SBurb came out, it suddenly went offline, and no further word or trace could be found of the original company. Exactly one week later, the FOP Game Server launched, and people... forgot about SBurb."
				""
				"&7What was it though? Well, I need to do some research... but explore deeper. See if you can find some Uranium Chunks for me... If you can, it'll confirm my suspicions."
			]
			dependencies: ["2019F6F56C5A7D4B"]
			id: "48F1C97A76078762"
			tasks: [{
				id: "63EC3F17062D9873"
				type: "item"
				item: "minestuck:raw_uranium"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "044DD37481499ADE"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Mysteriously Intact"
			x: -2.25d
			y: -2.5d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7I WAS right. Amazing!"
				""
				"&7Er, right then, what was SBurb? Well, it was basically a huge sandbox game. But instead of being 'digitized' and converted to data, the game was OVERLAYED on top of the real world. You could fight creatures, summon and build things, craft, join friends, etc. And eventually you could travel to other worlds, other places. Kind of like AoA's dimensions, but at the same time...not."
				""
				"&7And all of these was done in reality, in your own house, neighborhood, etc. The things you earned and built in the game, had physical presence. And you finding things from that game here..."
				""
				"&7You notice how the Cruxite and the special Uranium Ores weren't DLC gated? Even Coal Ore is locked behind DLC."
			]
			dependencies: ["48F1C97A76078762"]
			id: "1FCB0E4A2F267C82"
			tasks: [{
				id: "6C06E44CF1B7ADCC"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "The Temple of the Frog"
			x: -3.5d
			y: -1.25d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7If I'm right, and so far I have been, then you should be able to find a Frog Temple in the game server somewhere."
				""
				"&7Even though the FOP have altered the world and how it generates, things from SBurb should be unaffected. Which means... yes, you should be able to make the Temple Scanner!"
				""
				"&7Craft this scanner. It should help you locate a Frog Temple. You'll need it to access SBurb."
				""
				"&7You heard right. It's time we bring SBurb back!"
				""
				"&7Since the Frog Temple is fairly rare, you may need to travel far to find it. Use these Waystones to mark your base, and along your journey. You can teleport from any activated Waystone to another."
				""
				"&7You know, we should probably call SBurb something new... let's go with Minestuck. That sounds good."
			]
			dependencies: ["1FCB0E4A2F267C82"]
			id: "52754C14A4625112"
			tasks: [{
				id: "498E4416C31D09B0"
				type: "item"
				item: "minestuck:temple_scanner"
			}]
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "01D871E744042061"
					type: "choice"
					table_id: 2640422954496342337L
				}
				{
					id: "5B69E15E901DB066"
					type: "item"
					item: "waystones:waystone"
					count: 3
				}
			]
		}
		{
			title: "Lost Code in the Woods"
			x: -2.25d
			y: -1.25d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7Have you found the temple? At the top, inside, you should find a giant Lotus. Right Click it a few times to open it up."
				""
				"&7What did it give you... a book of SBurb Code? Yes, this is exactly what we need! And some Computer Parts, good!"
				""
				"&7But one book of SBURB Code isn't enough... Scanning the Lotus, it looks like it will regrow in about... 5 real minutes? Hang around for a bit. Explore the area. Then check back. "
				""
				"&7I estimate you'll need about 8 SBURB Code books to start getting the game back online. "
			]
			dependencies: ["52754C14A4625112"]
			id: "6A21DB08C3F1E5A7"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "746C6B880D44B4CF"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:sburb_code"
					count: 8L
				}
				{
					id: "126C1B10D4E2433C"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:computer_parts"
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "1D1B4EA005A717E9"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Where to Code?"
			x: -3.5d
			y: 0.0d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7Oh! That's what you can do while waiting!"
				""
				"&7You'll need somewhere to PUT the SBURB Code, right? If you explore some Dungeons, you may come across a Blank Disc. Those will work just fine."
				""
				"&7Or, you can go to the bottom of the Frog Temple, and search around for an opening. There should be a large chamber inside with pillars and... well, probably monsters. It's dark. "
				""
				"&7If you search around, you should be able to find some Blank Discs down there too. Just watch your step!"
			]
			dependencies: ["6A21DB08C3F1E5A7"]
			id: "0D54B906CCE3EE45"
			tasks: [{
				id: "21DAC55CF5E3DF32"
				type: "item"
				item: "minestuck:blank_disk"
				count: 2L
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "132308C580F62C39"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Server Planning"
			x: -2.25d
			y: 0.0d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7Okay Bandit, I've scanned over the SBURB Code Books and discussed with some of our Researchers here."
				""
				"&7You'll want to craft three things : The SBURB Client Disc, the SBURB Server Disc, and a SBURB Computer. If you have other assistants with you? You can get away with only ONE of you making a Server Disc, but the rest of you need the Computer and Client Disc."
				""
				"&7&lTHIS IS VERY IMPORTANT!&r &7You'll want to place the Computer in the center of a large area you plan on moving. "
				""
				"&7Because soon it's going to be moved by force. I'd say...30 block radius around the Computer will get moved?"
			]
			dependencies: ["0D54B906CCE3EE45"]
			id: "79F57A93686BD76B"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "680C4ACFAFED36E6"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:client_disk"
				}
				{
					id: "7C3798F60CA61DFD"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:server_disk"
				}
				{
					id: "223B083645EC3DD5"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:computer"
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "1244515E126514D8"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 5632731352558517809L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Building Up"
			x: -1.0d
			y: 0.0d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7Okay, got the SBURB Computer placed? Good. Now Right Click the Client and Server Discs onto the Computer to install them. Then Right Click the Computer to turn it on and then access the interface."
				""
				"&7The button in the upper right will swap you between Client and Server options. First you'll want to Select Color. Then you'll want to set the Server to Open to Clients. Then you'll want to connect with the Client."
				""
				"&7Now in the Server section, you can enter Edit Mode. You'll pop out of your body and the inventory will be different. You'll want to move the Cruxtruder, Totem Lathe, and Alchemiter to your hotbar and build them close by."
				""
				"&7And  you'll want to take that Captchalogue Card and drop it onto the ground with Q. Then you can exit Edit Mode by hitting X on your keyboard and pick it up."
			]
			dependencies: ["79F57A93686BD76B"]
			id: "415FC4F6B22EA0F7"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5842C390D44BC87A"
				type: "item"
				item: {
					id: "minestuck:captcha_card"
					Count: 1b
					tag: {
						punched: 1b
						contentID: "minestuck:cruxite_apple"
					}
				}
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "6EF1761680E54AF8"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Beginning Alchemy"
			x: -1.0d
			y: -1.25d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7Now that you have all these machines, what to do with them? Well, first you'll want to go over to the Cruxtruder and take the Lid off. It's the 3x3 square platform looking one. Just break the lid off with your Pickaxe to open it up. "
				""
				"&7Now Right Click some Cruxite onto the opening, then Right Click the wheel on one side. You'll get a Cruxite Dowel in the color you chose earlier!"
				""
				"&7Now that Captchalogue Card? Take it over to the Totem Lathe. On one side is the green SBURB Symbol. There's a slot you can Right Click that Captchalogue Card into. Then Right Click the Cruxite Dowel into the open space to the right of the SBURB Symbol."
				""
				"&7Now, there's a gray square above the placed Cruxite Dowel. Right Click that to 'carve' the Dowel. This is the first step in basic Alchemy for SBURB... I mean Minestuck."
			]
			dependencies: ["415FC4F6B22EA0F7"]
			id: "10E2B9F70E803BDB"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "28A6A35006F1B26F"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:cruxtruder_lid"
				}
				{
					id: "7EA55ECA3223D4E4"
					type: "item"
					item: {
						id: "minestuck:cruxite_dowel"
						Count: 1b
						tag: {
							contentID: "minestuck:cruxite_apple"
						}
					}
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "10E83500EF2C7681"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "First Artifact"
			x: -1.0d
			y: -2.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7There's a lotta steps here, I know, but once you get the hang of it..."
				""
				"&7That Cruxite Dowel that now looks like an Hourglass? It's labeled with (Cruxite Artifact). That is what will be made when you Alchemize it. "
				""
				"&7The larger 4x4 platform is the Alchemiter. There's a tower on one corner with a platform, where you can place the Cruxite Dowel on. Then you can Right Click the platform and alchemize the Cruxite Artifact : a Cruxite Apple (Or sometimes a bottle)"
				""
				"&7&lDON'T EAT THE APPLE YET! You need to do a bit of prep first!"
			]
			dependencies: ["10E2B9F70E803BDB"]
			id: "5C1E778DADF0B55B"
			tasks: [{
				id: "3574D5438A7AF261"
				type: "item"
				item: "minestuck:cruxite_apple"
			}]
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "6DBF91BA59E38657"
					type: "choice"
					table_id: 2640422954496342337L
				}
				{
					id: "0B71F8154E850066"
					type: "item"
					item: "waystones:waystone"
					count: 2
				}
			]
		}
		{
			x: 0.25d
			y: -2.5d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7Okay, I have a small checklist for you before you consume that Cruxite Artifact : "
				""
				"&71) Is your SBURB Computer inside a protected building? Much like protecting yourself against zombies, skeletons, etc. Make sure it is inside."
				""
				"&72) Do you have a bunch of storage in this building? Do you have a lot of supplies in them? Food, Iron, Copper, Saplings, etc."
				""
				"&73) Do you have any activated Waystones away from your Base? Make sure you put one down more than 30 blocks away from the SBURB Computer and &lACTIVATE IT&r&7, don't forget!"
				""
				"&74) Do you have an unused Waystone in your inventory?"
				""
				"&75) Do you have a weapon and some decent (Iron level) armor?"
			]
			dependencies: ["5C1E778DADF0B55B"]
			id: "3C01B17B8602B0C8"
			tasks: [{
				id: "55158453D8816F2E"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "Departure Checklist"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "678ED7B253B4EDAC"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			x: 1.5d
			y: -2.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7You all armed and armored, Bandit? Got your Waystone, a snack, etc? All your doors closed? Yes? Good? Time to eat that Cruxite Artifact!"
				""
				"&7You'll notice that eating the Artifact will... ask you for a title. This title will change how your part of The Medium, basically the base world of Minestuck, will generate. You can choose something that sounds neat, or just hit Random. When you accept your title, you and the area around your SBURB Computer will be moved to The Medium."
				""
				"&7Now you get to see if you made a decent enough base and remembered to close all your doors. The land you took with you will appear high above the Medium, and on it Imps will constantly spawn. These dangerous little creatures can wear you down fast, so be careful."
				""
				"&7What they also do is drop Grist, a resource that you need for building and Alchemizing."
			]
			dependencies: ["3C01B17B8602B0C8"]
			id: "3C99F25DDE417366"
			tasks: [{
				id: "303B78BF19033696"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "To the Medium"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Alchemy Realized"
			x: 0.25d
			y: -1.25d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7Now that you're in The Medium and have secured your base, it's time to open up Minestuck fully, and begin use it fully."
				""
				"&7It seems that so much of the FOP Game Server is built on top of layers and layers of lost, half deleted, broken, and ignored systems. And at the lowest level? The original SBURB. So much of this Medium and worlds beyond collect the remnants of lost systems : This is what Grist is, the lost resources of everything. This is why it's called Minestuck now, its stuck at the bottom, and no longer the same as it was."
				""
				"&7And you can use this Grist to craft almost anything in FOP Game system. But to do that, you'll need one more SBURB Alchemy machine: the Punch Designix."
				""
				"&7Go over to your SBURB Computer and enter Editing mode again. You'll see the Punch Designix available, but it'll cost 4 of a specific kind of Grist. This is usually tied to the Imps that spawn on your land."
			]
			dependencies: ["3C99F25DDE417366"]
			id: "70B74F6AC7AFFA80"
			tasks: [{
				id: "3DC64399EBD4D028"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "Of Alchemy and Gateways"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "426652A169FD6E8C"
				type: "item"
				item: "minecraft:mossy_cobblestone"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Captcha'd"
			x: 1.5d
			y: -1.25d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7That Mossy Cobblestone I just gave you? Put it in your Hotbar and hold it in your hand and press V. Poof, gone!"
				""
				"&7Actually, what you did is add it to your Minestuck Sylladex. Your sylladex is a... sort of special inventory made of Captchalogue Cards. Each card can store up to a stack of a single item. And you can craft more Captchalogue Cards and add them to your Sylladex."
				""
				"&7To access your Sylladex (as well as your Grist Cache), hit G. The first tab is your Sylladex. You can add more Cards here, or open up the Sylladex with the button."
				""
				"&7Your Sylladex starts in Queue-Mode (shown in the upper right). Meaning that you Add items from right to left, and can take items only from the right most card (by Left clicking the item itself)."
				""
				"&7But if you Right Click, you remove the Captchalogue Card WITH the item on it!"
			]
			dependencies: ["70B74F6AC7AFFA80"]
			id: "679B9480C543F403"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "09894FCD2FC3A9D8"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:captcha_card"
				}
				{
					id: "24AB8EF77ADE7D7F"
					type: "item"
					title: "Captchalogue Card with 1 Mossy Cobblestone"
					item: {
						id: "minestuck:captcha_card"
						Count: 1b
						tag: {
							punched: 0b
							contentID: "minecraft:mossy_cobblestone"
							contentSize: 1
						}
					}
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "3DC3901F15850189"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Punch It, Alchemy!"
			x: 0.25d
			y: 0.0d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7Now you have a Captchalogue Card with a Mossy Cobblestone in it. You (should) have a bunch of blank Captchalogue Cards. And you have all these Alchemy machines. So, how do you Alchemize up some more Mossy Cobblestone?"
				""
				"&7First, go over to the Punch Designix. Right Click an empty Captchaloge Card on the front left side of it, where you can see a slot. Then, Right Click the Captchalogue Card with the Mossy Cobblestone onto the Keyboard on the front right side."
				""
				"&7This will make the empty Captchalogue Card in the Designix (Punched) with the Mossy Cobblestone design... much like your Cruxite Artifact started on a (Punched) Captchalogue Card!"
				""
				"&7Like with the Artifact, put Cruxite into the Cruxtruder and make a Dowel. Then place the Dowel and the (Punched) Card into the Totem Lathe, shape the Dowel, and then bring it to the Alchemiter to Alchemize up 10 more."
			]
			dependencies: ["679B9480C543F403"]
			id: "0B913EC0A71D77DA"
			tasks: [{
				id: "450C6FCF2DDB3F40"
				type: "item"
				item: "minecraft:mossy_cobblestone"
				count: 10L
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "42410B896074BA93"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			x: 1.5d
			y: 0.0d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7Like I mentioned, entering The Medium brings the land with you. Now, have you looked up yet? Directly up from your SBURB Computer."
				""
				"&7High up you should see TWO colored rings spinning. These are the Gates, your paths to and from the main land, where you can find more Grist and other important supplies."
				""
				"&7You'll want to build up to the lower circle, and build a platform under it. Then you REALLY should build a platform up under the higher gate! You'll understand why later."
				""
				"&7Before you enter the first (lower) gate, make sure you are armed, armored, and have food. Because you'll be fighting pretty fast when you drop onto the main land."
				""
				"&7To get back to your land, look near where the first Gate drops you. There should be a plain Stone pillar with another Gate on top."
			]
			dependencies: ["0B913EC0A71D77DA"]
			id: "0029F0BC75976423"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7491809FAFDDE7AB"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "The Gates"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Advanced Alchemy"
			x: 2.75d
			y: 1.25d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7Alright, you know the basics of alchemy : Captchalogue an item, Punch it onto a card in the Designix, Carve that on a Dowel in the Totem Lathe, then use Grist at the Alchemizer to create it."
				""
				"&7But also, there are two ways of COMBINING Unpunched and (Punched) Cards into brand new items : With the Designix, or with the Totem Lathe."
				""
				"&7Example, a Rock Cookie. You can take a (Punched) Cobblestone card and a (Punched) Cookie card, and put both of them into the Totem Lathe. This will make a Rock Cookie shaped Cruxite Dowel. This is known as \\&\\&\\ (and) Alchemy."
				""
				"&7Another Example : Flowery Mossy Cobblestone. If you place a (Punched) Mossy Cobblestone card into the Designix (instead of a blank card!), and Right Click an UNPUNCHED Captchalogue Card with a Flower in it onto the keyboard, it'll punch the design onto the Mossy Cobblestone card. This is called || (or) alchemy."
			]
			dependencies: ["0029F0BC75976423"]
			id: "4EAEC7D5C5DD1893"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "7EC8A51A321E0B04"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:rock_cookie"
				}
				{
					id: "38F8B3143405CE9D"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:flowery_mossy_cobblestone"
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "2CD0CBCFFF3367EF"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "A Solid Note"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 0.0d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7If a Book and Quill aren't 'solid' enough for you to write messages to other assistants, you could always Alchemy up a Stone Tablet and a Carving Tool!"
				""
				"&7Put the Carving Tool in your offhand, and Right Click while holding the Stone Tablet. Now you can write, I mean carve, a message!"
				""
				"&7Now normally you could place this Stone Tablet out like any other block, but it seems to interact weirdly with FOP's servers and causes... issues, so I suggest NOT doing that."
			]
			dependencies: ["4EAEC7D5C5DD1893"]
			id: "47B542CF3816510F"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "3105B5E43AB4CB6F"
