		{
			title: "Basic Sylladex Modus"
			x: 12.75d
			y: 0.0d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7Like I mentioned, your Sylladex starts off in Queue mode. Things get added to the left side, and can only be taken out of the right side."
				""
				"&7But you can change the mode of how items are stored and retrieved from your Sylladex by changing its Modus. The other simple Modus you can swap to is Stack."
				""
				"&7With Stack Modus, its like a stack of books. You add an item to the left, and can only take the left most item."
				""
				"&7To change the Modus of your Sylladex, take the Modus card, and hit G to open your Minestuck menu. Place the new Modus card into the Sylladex spot you usually add new Captchalogue cards to, and hit Use Item. It'll swap the new Modus in and your old Modus out."
			]
			dependencies: ["679B9480C543F403"]
			id: "3357D6C93A0DEB53"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "7390353C501E9327"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:queue_modus_card"
				}
				{
					id: "4A7CE8D037F2FDF3"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:stack_modus_card"
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "1912FB3CCF2AFF49"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Alternate Modus"
			x: 12.75d
			y: 1.25d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7With Alchemy, you can create a few different Modus for your Sylladex."
				""
				"&7The Queue-Stack Modus combines the two. Items are added to the left side, and the Left most AND the Right most items can be removed."
				""
				"&7The Tree Modus is.... very different. The first item added is the Root. When another item is added, it gets sorted alphabetically, to one of two branches (if it comes before or after the Root alphabetically)"
				""
				"&7When the Root has two 'branches', the next item added goes to the left most 'branch' available, becoming either the left or right branch alphabetically."
				""
				"&7Each 'branch' can branch out to two cards. Those cards can branch out again. And again. The last card of every branch is called a Leaf."
				""
				"&7Leaf cards can be pulled out freely. But removing a Branch or Root will cause all cards under it to drop."
			]
			dependencies: [
				"3357D6C93A0DEB53"
				"4EAEC7D5C5DD1893"
			]
			id: "450FD08EFACAD8BC"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "44870CF436A379B2"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:queuestack_modus_card"
				}
				{
					id: "10F4D4589D686403"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:tree_modus_card"
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "6C3A1553D5E7F885"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 5632731352558517809L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Interesting Modus"
			x: 12.75d
			y: 2.5d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7Set Modus has the benefit of letting you pull any item in it when you want, no messing with Stacks or Queues."
				""
				"&7The downside? You can only have one of a specific item at a time. "
				""
				"&7Alternatively, you can use the Hashmap Modus. Every item's name can be converted into a Hash, a sort of math formula derived thing."
				""
				"&7While this one lets you keep up to a stack of an item, you cannot keep more as multiple Captchalogue cards cannot have the same Hash. This also means different items with the same name, or even rarely some items with different names, may have the same Hash."
			]
			dependencies: ["450FD08EFACAD8BC"]
			id: "2D44BE5D2DDBF4E9"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "585BA7D3AC1EB593"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:set_modus_card"
				}
				{
					id: "3279A2D11DE9BE0C"
					type: "item"
					item: "minestuck:hashmap_modus_card"
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "0D360B3796A3CDF3"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 5632731352558517809L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Good Alchemical Drinks"
			x: 6.5d
			y: 1.25d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&7I'd normally say something like \"What is Alchemy but mixing liquids?\" but that doesn't really work with Minestuck Alchemy, since its about Captchaloguing, Punching Cards, and Lathing Totems. "
				""
				"&7But yes even with Alchemization, you can make some pretty tasty drinks!"
				""
				"&7There are a lot flavors of Faygo beyond the goold ol purple one. I'm just partial to that one."
				""
				"&7And Orange. Mmm orange."
